title: First <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> Congress
subtitle: The future of this new party will be decided here.
view-if: concord_formed
on-arrival: {!

if (Q.in_social_catholic_coalition) Q.concord_left += 5;
if (Q.peoples_party) Q.concord_left += 3;
if (Q.left_split) Q.concord_left += 1;
if (Q.sapd_formed) Q.concord_left += 2;
if (Q.reformist_strength >= Q.left_strength + Q.center_strength) {
    Q.concord_left += 2;
} else {
    Q.concord_right += 2;
}
if (Q.nationalization_adopted || Q.economic_democracy) {
    Q.concord_right += 3;
    Q.concord_right += Q.economic_democracy*2;
}

Q.labor_right_points = 0;
Q.conservative_right_points = 0;
Q.catholic_center_points = 0;
Q.agrarian_right_points = 0;
Q.tory_democratic_points = 0;
Q.labor_left_points = 0;

Q.labor_points_lead = 0; 
Q.democratic_points_lead = 0;
Q.presidential_points_lead = 0;
Q.concord_deadlock = 0;
Q.labor_right_points_lead = 0;
Q.conservative_right_points_lead = 0;
Q.catholic_center_points_lead = 0;
Q.agrarian_right_points_lead = 0;
Q.tory_democratic_points_lead = 0;
Q.labor_left_points_lead = 0;

Q.treviranus_unlock = 0;
Q.adenauer_unlock = 0;
Q.lambach_unlock = 0;
Q.stegerwald_unlock = 0;
Q.gereke_unlock = 0;

if (Q.traditionalist_leader == "Lambach") {
    Q.concord_right += 10;
}

if (Q.concord_right >= (Q.concord_left + 5)) {
    Q.concord_ideology = "Right"
} else if (Q.concord_left >= (Q.concord_right + 5)) {
    Q.concord_ideology = "Left"
} else {
    Q.concord_ideology = "Moderate"
}

if (Q.concord_ideology == "Right") {
    Q.labor_right_points += 3;
    Q.conservative_right_points += 5;
    Q.agrarian_right_points += 3;
} else if (Q.concord_ideology == "Moderate") {
    Q.tory_democratic_points += 3;
    Q.catholic_center_points += 1;
    Q.labor_right_points += 1;
    Q.labor_left_points += 1;
    Q.agrarian_right_points += 1;
    Q.conservative_right_points += 1;
} else if (Q.concord_ideology == "Left") {
    Q.catholic_center_points += 5;
    Q.tory_democratic_points += 3;
    Q.labor_left_points += 5;
}

if (Q.traditionalist_gold_formed || Q.concord_gold_formed) {
    Q.gold_in_concord = 1;
    Q.tory_democratic_points += 4;
}


if (Q.traditionalist_leader == "Lambach" && !Q.lambach_bonus) {
    Q.labor_right_points += 6;
    Q.lambach_bonus = 1;
}

if (Q.unionist_leader == "Sedgewick" && !Q.stegerwald_bonus) {
    Q.labor_left_points += 8;
    Q.stegerwald_bonus = 1;
}

if (Q.unionist_leader == "Aldermoor" && !Q.adenauer_bonus) {
    Q.catholic_center_points += 6;
    Q.adenauer_bonus = 1;
}

if (Q.welfare <= 0) {
    Q.labor_left_points += 3;
    Q.labor_right_points += 3;
}

if (Q.unions_independent) {
    Q.labor_right_points += 5;
    Q.labor_left_points += 5;
}

if (Q.commons_unionist_normalized) {
    Q.labor_right_points += Q.commons_unionist_normalized * ((100 - Q.pro_republic) / 200);
    Q.labor_left_points += Q.commons_unionist_normalized * (Q.pro_republic / 200);
    if (Q.traditionalist_leader == "Lambach") {
        Q.labor_right_points += Q.commons_unionist_normalized * ((100 - Q.pro_republic) / 200);
    }
}

if (Q.burgher_unionist_normalized || Q.guild_unionist_normalized) {
    Q.conservative_right_points += (Q.burgher_unionist_normalized + Q.guild_unionist_normalized) * ((100 - Q.pro_republic) / 200);
    Q.tory_democratic_points += (Q.burgher_unionist_normalized + Q.guild_unionist_normalized) * (Q.pro_republic / 200);
}

if (Q.landed_unionist_normalized) {
    Q.agrarian_right_points += Q.landed_unionist_normalized * ((100 - Q.pro_republic) / 200);
}

if (Q.faithful_unionist_normalized) {
    Q.catholic_center_points += Q.faithful_unionist_normalized * (Q.pro_republic / 400);
    Q.conservative_right_points += Q.faithful_unionist_normalized * ((100 - Q.pro_republic) / 400);
}

if (Q.unionist_relation >= 20) {
    Q.labor_left_points += (Q.unionist_relation / 10);
    Q.catholic_center_points += (Q.unionist_relation / 10);
    Q.tory_democratic_points += (Q.unionist_relation / 20);
} else {
    Q.labor_right_points += ((20 - Q.unionist_relation) / 5);
    Q.conservative_right_points += ((20 - Q.unionist_relation) / 5);
    Q.agrarian_right_points += ((20 - Q.unionist_relation) / 5);
}

if (Q.land_reform || Q.tariffs < 0) {
    Q.agrarian_right_points += Q.land_reform*5;
    Q.agrarian_right_points += (Q.tariffs*-1)*5;
}

if (Q.gold_reform && !Q.lvp_formed && Q.gold_exist) {
    Q.tory_democratic_points += Q.gold_votes;
} else if (Q.gold_reform && Q.lvp_formed && Q.gold_exist) {
    Q.tory_democratic_points += Q.lvp_votes / 2;
}

Q.labor_points = Q.labor_right_points + Q.labor_left_points;
if (Q.labor_points) {
    Q.labor_right_points *= 0.5;
    Q.labor_left_points *= 0.5;
}
Q.labor_points = Q.labor_right_points + Q.labor_left_points;
Q.unionist_points = Q.labor_left_points + Q.catholic_center_points;
Q.democratic_points = Q.labor_left_points + Q.catholic_center_points + Q.tory_democratic_points;
Q.presidential_points = Q.labor_right_points + Q.conservative_right_points + Q.agrarian_right_points;
Q.traditionalist_points = Q.conservative_right_points + Q.agrarian_right_points + Q.tory_democratic_points + Q.labor_right_points;

if ((Q.labor_points - 3) > Q.conservative_right_points && (Q.labor_points - 3) > Q.catholic_center_points && (Q.labor_points - 3) > Q.agrarian_right_points && (Q.labor_points - 3) > Q.tory_democratic_points) {
    Q.labor_points_lead = 1;
    if (Q.labor_left_points >= Q.labor_right_points) {
        Q.labor_left_points_lead = 1;
        Q.labor_right_points_lead = 0;
    } else if (Q.labor_right_points > Q.labor_left_points) {
        Q.labor_left_points_lead = 0;
        Q.labor_right_points_lead = 1;
    }
} else {
    Q.labor_points_lead = 0;
}

if ((Q.democratic_points - 5) > Q.presidential_points) {
    Q.democratic_points_lead = 1;
    if (Q.tory_democratic_points >= Q.unionist_points) {
        Q.tory_democratic_points_lead = 1;
        Q.catholic_center_points_lead = 0;
    } else if (Q.unionist_points > Q.tory_democratic_points) {
        Q.tory_democratic_points_lead = 0;
        Q.catholic_center_points_lead = 1;
    }
} else {
    Q.democratic_points_lead = 0;
}

if ((Q.presidential_points - 5) > Q.democratic_points) {
    Q.presidential_points_lead = 1;
    if (!Q.labor_right_points_lead) {
        if (Q.conservative_right_points >= Q.labor_right_points && Q.conservative_right_points >= Q.agrarian_right_points) {
            Q.conservative_right_points_lead = 1;
            Q.agrarian_right_points_lead = 0;
            Q.labor_right_points_lead = 0;
        } else if (Q.labor_right_points >= Q.conservative_right_points && Q.labor_right_points >= Q.agrarian_right_points) {
            Q.conservative_right_points_lead = 0;
            Q.labor_right_points_lead = 1;
            Q.agrarian_right_points_lead = 0;
        } else if (Q.agrarian_right_points >= Q.conservative_right_points && Q.agrarian_right_points >= Q.labor_right_points) {
            Q.conservative_right_points_lead = 0;
            Q.labor_right_points_lead = 0;
            Q.agrarian_right_points_lead = 1;
        }
    }
} else {
    Q.presidential_points_lead = 0;
}

if (Q.democratic_points_lead && Q.tory_democratic_points_lead) {
    Q.treviranus_unlock = 1;
} else if (Q.democratic_points_lead && Q.catholic_center_points_lead) {
    Q.adenauer_unlock = 1;
} else if (Q.presidential_points_lead) {
    Q.gereke_unlock = 1;
}

if (Q.labor_left_points_lead) {
    Q.stegerwald_unlock = 1;
    Q.treviranus_unlock = 0;
    Q.adenauer_unlock = 0;
    Q.gereke_unlock = 0;
    Q.lambach_unlock = 0;
} else if (Q.labor_right_points_lead) {
    Q.stegerwald_unlock = 0;
    Q.treviranus_unlock = 0;
    Q.adenauer_unlock = 0;
    Q.gereke_unlock = 0;
    Q.lambach_unlock = 1;
}

if (!Q.treviranus_unlock && !Q.adenauer_unlock && !Q.gereke_unlock && !Q.lambach_unlock && !Q.stegerwald_unlock) {
    Q.concord_deadlock = 1;
} else {
    Q.concord_deadlock = 0;
}


!}
on-departure: guild_unionist = 30 if guild_unionist < 30; landed_unionist = 30 if landed_unionist < 30
max-visits: 1
tags: event
face-image: img/cvp.jpg
new-page: true

= First <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> Congress

The <span style="color: #000000;">Christian People's Party</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>) has officially been founded! Adam Sedgewick, orchestrator of this arrangement and leader of the former <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>, has been chosen as the interim leader of the new party.

The <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>'s inaugural congress will play a major role in shaping the direction of the newly founded party, and to elect a new chairman. It finally looks like we might have some competition now.

- @cvp_factions

@cvp_factions
title: The party congress is held.
subtitle: The factions of the two parties shall reorganize into blocs.

The merger of the two parties also brings together the many factions of the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span> and the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>. Though they now share a party banner, deep factional divides remain, and infighting continues to plague the new organization—at least until the party congress settles the balance of power.

The reorganized factions are as follows:

<span style="color: #003755;">Far-Right Protestants</span> (<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>) - ??? - [? if (concord_ideology != "Right" or royalist_votes < 35): Fringe ?][? if (concord_ideology == "Right" and royalist_votes >= 30): Marginal ?]

<span style="color: #3E3B2D;">Far-Right Catholics</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**Unionists**</span>) - ??? - [? if (concord_ideology != "Right" or royalist_votes < 30): Fringe ?][? if (concord_ideology == "Right" and royalist_votes >= 30): Marginal ?]

<span style="color: #3E88B3;">National Conservatives</span> (<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>) - Gereke - [? if concord_ideology == "Left": Marginal?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and not presidential_points_lead: Limited?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and presidential_points_lead and not conservative_right_points_lead: Influential?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and conservative_right_points_lead: Powerful?]

<span style="color: #385A38;">Agrarians</span> (<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>) - Gereke - [? if concord_ideology == "Left": Marginal?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and not presidential_points_lead: Limited?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and presidential_points_lead: Relevant?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and agrarian_right_points_lead: Influential?]

<hr id="read-marker">
<span style="color: #6D5298;">Christian Socials</span> (<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>) - Lambach - [? if concord_ideology == "Left" and not labor_points_lead: Marginal?][? if ((concord_ideology != "Left" and not presidential_points_lead and not labor_points_lead) or (concord_ideology == "Left" and labor_points_lead)): Limited?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and presidential_points_lead and not labor_points_lead: Relevant?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and labor_points_lead and not labor_right_points_lead: Influential?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and labor_right_points_lead: Powerful?]

<span style="color: #330000;">Catholic Labor</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**Unionists**</span>) - Sedgewick - [? if concord_ideology == "Left" and labor_left_points_lead: Powerful?][? if (concord_ideology == "Left" and not labor_left_points_lead) or labor_points_lead: Influential?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and democratic_points_lead and not labor_points_lead: Relevant?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and not democratic_points_lead and not labor_points_lead: Limited?]
<hr id="read-marker">
<span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservatives</span> (<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>) - Trevannon - [? if concord_ideology == "Left" and democratic_points_lead: Dominant?][? if ((concord_ideology == "Left" and not democratic_points_lead) or (democratic_points_lead and concord_ideology != "Left")): Influential?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and not democratic_points_lead: Relevant?]

<span style="color: #000099;">Catholic Right</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**Unionists**</span>) - Trevannon - [? if concord_ideology == "Left" and democratic_points_lead: Influential?][? if ((concord_ideology == "Left" and not democratic_points_lead) or (democratic_points_lead and concord_ideology != "Left")): Relevant?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and not democratic_points_lead: Limited?]

[? if concord_gold_formed: <span style="color: #D8B868;">Strattonites</span> (<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>) - Trevannon - [? if concord_ideology == "Left" and democratic_points_lead: Relevant?][? if ((concord_ideology == "Left" and not democratic_points_lead) or (democratic_points_lead and concord_ideology != "Left")): Limited?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and not democratic_points_lead: Marginal?]?]

[? if concord_gold_formed: <span style="color: #8C7A3C;">Industrialists</span> (<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>) - Trevannon - [? if concord_ideology != "Left" and not labor_points_lead: Influential?][? if not (concord_ideology != "Left" and not labor_points_lead): Relevant?]?]
<hr id="read-marker">
<span style="color: #000000;">the Unionists</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**Unionists**</span>) - Aldermoor - [? if concord_ideology == "Left" and democratic_points_lead: Powerful?][? if ((concord_ideology == "Left" and not democratic_points_lead) or (democratic_points_lead and concord_ideology != "Left")): Influential?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and not democratic_points_lead: Relevant?]

<span style="color: #FF7F00;">Christian Left</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**Unionists**</span>) - Aldermoor / Sedgewick - [? if concord_ideology == "Left" and labor_left_points_lead: Relevant?][? if concord_ideology == "Left" and not labor_left_points_lead: Limited?][? if concord_ideology != "Left": Marginal?]
<hr id="read-marker">
[? if labor_points_lead: The Christian trade unions have found themselves at an advantageous position going into the congress. ?][? if democratic_points_lead: The pro-<span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> forces have found themselves at an advantageous position going into the congress. ?][? if presidential_points_lead: The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span> forces have found themselves at an advantageous position going into the congress. ?][? if concord_deadlock: No faction seems able to secure a significant plurality of support within the party, so a compromise candidate is expected to emerge. ?]

The vote for the party's leadership has begun.

- @stegerwald
- @lambach
- @adenauer
- @gereke
- @treviranus
- @compromise

@stegerwald
title: Adam Sedgewick, formerly of the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>, is elected, no longer an interim leader.
subtitle: Sedgewick is relatively moderate, and his trade union roots are good news for our cooperation. - <span style="color: #000000;">Catholic Labor</span> Wing
unavailable-subtitle: Sedgewick is seen as too friendly toward us, and the party needs a new face. - <span style="color: #000000;">Catholic Labor</span> Wing
choose-if: stegerwald_unlock
on-arrival: unionist_relation += 15; pro_republic += 5; ddp_relation += 5; gold_relation += 5; lvp_relation += 5; commons_unionist += 5; disfavored_unionist += 3; commons_marcher -= 3; commons_collectivist -= 2; disfavored_marcher -= 3; landed_unionist -= 4; guild_unionist -= 4; landed_dnf += 4; guild_dnf += 4; faithful_unionist += 8; concord_leader = "Sedgewick"; concord_left += 5; concord_ideology = "Left"; guild_unionist = 25 if guild_unionist < 25; landed_unionist = 25 if landed_unionist < 25
face-image: img/portraits/stegerwald.jpg

Somewhat surprisingly, <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span> leader Adam Sedgewick is elected as the chairman of its successor party. This is largely attributed to the unified support from the various Christian labor unions and backing from former <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span> and Catholic politicians. However, he remains largely opposed by former <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> members due to his willingness to cooperate constructively with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>.

It was widely expected that, with the merger of the two parties, politicians like Sedgewick would shift to the left wing of the newly created party—and this has indeed proven true. His strongest supporters, aside from the trade unions, include the now strengthened <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Christian Left</span> faction, which will push for a paternalistic economic policy and greater cooperation with the <span style="color: #c00000;">socialists</span>. Sedgewick is also a committed <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span>, a stance that has pushed some ardent monarchists over to the <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span>.

@lambach
title: Walther Lambach, formerly of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span>, is elected as their new leader.
subtitle: Lambach was apart of the <span style="color: #6D5298;">Christian Social</span> wing in the former <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span>. - <span style="color: #6D5298;">Christian Social</span> Wing
unavailable-subtitle: Lambach and his trade unions face significant animosity from the broader party, particularly the industrialist backers - <span style="color: #6D5298;">Christian Social</span> Wing.
choose-if: lambach_unlock
on-arrival: unionist_relation -= 5; pro_republic -= 5; ddp_relation += 8; gold_relation += 8; lvp_relation += 8; commons_unionist += 10; disfavored_unionist += 5; commons_dnf -= 3; commons_royalist -= 3; commons_marcher -= 3; commons_collectivist -= 2; disfavored_marcher -= 3; disfavored_dnf -= 3; disfavored_royalist -= 3; landed_unionist -= 10; burgher_unionist += 4; burgher_marcher -= 4; guild_unionist -= 10; landed_dnf += 4; guild_dnf += 4; landed_gold += 6; landed_lvp += 8; landed_ddp += 2; guild_gold += 6; guild_ddp += 2; guild_lvp += 8; faithful_unionist -= 6; faithful_marcher += 4; faithful_gold += 2; faithful_lvp += 4; faithful_ddp += 2; concord_leader = "Lambach"; concord_right += 5; concord_ideology = "Right"; guild_unionist = 25 if guild_unionist < 25; landed_unionist = 25 if landed_unionist < 25
face-image: img/portraits/LambachWalther.jpg
achievement: christlicher_sozialismus

Somehow, the <span style="color: #6D5298;">Christian Social</span> wing, now diluted within a much larger party, has managed to elect one of their own as the leader of the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>. Walther Lambach, the writer of the Lambach article years ago[? if traditionalist_leader == "Lambach":, and the most recent leader of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?], has won the vote largely due to the unified support of the Christian labor unions, who strongly back his vision for a *Volksgemeinschaft*.

More <span style="color: #c00000;">worker-friendly</span> policies have been added to the platform, such as expanding social welfare, increasing pensions, and implementing more progressive income taxes. They've even rejected austerity as a solution to the Commonwealth's current economic crisis, instead voicing support for public works. However, this has significantly strained industrial enthusiasm for the formation of the new party, and they have begun redirecting funds toward the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span>.

This, however, is not good news for us. <span style="color: #6D5298;">Christian Social</span> ideology is deeply rooted in antisemitism, racism, nationalism, and religiosity. If anything, we've noticed worsening relations with the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>, as they attempt to present a non-<span style="color: #9B0000;">Marxist</span> alternative to the workers.

@adenauer
title: Konrad Aldermoor, formerly of the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>, is elected as their new leader.
subtitle: Aldermoor, a long-time advocate for 'leaving the tower' and Mayor of Cologne since the Republic's inception - <span style="color: #000000;">the Unionists</span> Wing
unavailable-subtitle: [? if stegerwald_unlock or lambach_unlock: Aldermoor lacks the broad appeal needed, and the party prefers to back a Labor candidate instead. ?][? if not stegerwald_unlock and not lambach_unlock: Aldermoor lacks the popular appeal needed for leadership, and the party prefers to back a more right-wing candidate instead. ?] - <span style="color: #000000;">the Unionists</span> Wing
choose-if: adenauer_unlock
on-arrival: pro_republic += 5; unionist_relation += 5; ddp_relation += 3; gold_relation += 3; lvp_relation += 3; commons_unionist += 3; disfavored_unionist += 3; commons_dnf -= 1; commons_royalist -= 2; disfavored_dnf -= 2; disfavored_royalist -= 2; landed_unionist -= 3; burgher_unionist += 3; burgher_other -= 3; guild_unionist -= 5; landed_dnf += 3; guild_dnf += 3; faithful_unionist += 5; faithful_royalist -= 3; faithful_dnf -= 2; concord_leader = "Aldermoor"; concord_left += 3; concord_ideology = "Left"; guild_unionist = 25 if guild_unionist < 25; landed_unionist = 25 if landed_unionist < 25
face-image: img/portraits/adenauer.jpg

# support losses are because he is a c*tholic

Konrad Aldermoor, the long-time Mayor of Cologne, has been elevated to the leadership of one of the Commonwealth's largest parties, which he strongly supported the formation of. Aldermoor is committed to democratic principles and sits on the right wing of the former <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>, without being tied to Christian labor. This has granted him the ability to rally a broad coalition of party leaders around his calm and stabilizing leadership against the more fringe politicians of the party.

With his slogan 'No Experiments!', we do not expect any major changes to the party program under his leadership, fostering a sense among the people that the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> is a pole of stability that the Commonwealth people can rally behind. In terms of our relationship with the <span style="color: #000000;">Christians</span>, Aldermoor, being a former <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span> member, is relatively more friendly toward us than many others to his right. We can also count on the pressure from the <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Christian Left</span>, who, similar to the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s left wing historically, are powerless to enact changes to the left but are influential in preventing changes to the right.

@gereke
title: Günther Gereke, formerly of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span>, is elected as their new leader.
subtitle: Gereke has significant influence over the agricultural and industrial establishment, being a key member of the RLB and a founder of another rural association. - <span style="color: #3E88B3;">National Conservative</span> and <span style="color: #385A38;">Agrarian</span> Wing
unavailable-subtitle: A new face, but associated too much with the Westmore elements on the right-wing. - <span style="color: #3E88B3;">National Conservative</span> and <span style="color: #385A38;">Agrarian</span> Wing
choose-if: gereke_unlock
on-arrival: unionist_relation -= 15; concord_right += 5; nationalism += 5; pro_republic -= 5; burgher_unionist += 3; guild_unionist += 6; landed_unionist += 12; landed_other *= 0.3; landed_dnf -= 3; guild_dnf -= 5; burgher_dnf -= 3; faithful_unionist -= 6; faithful_marcher += 6; unionist_r += other_r*0.3; other_r = other_r*0.7; concord_leader = "Gereke"; concord_ideology = "Right"; guild_unionist = 25 if guild_unionist < 25; landed_unionist = 25 if landed_unionist < 25
face-image: img/portraits/gereke.jpg

Günther Gereke, a lawyer and prominent politician from rural the Commonwealth, has been elected as the new leader of the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>. What makes him notable is that he is an <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> politician from west of the Elbe River, a leading reformist economic theorist, and someone with close ties to General Kurt von Staal. He bears similarities to Trevannon, though he is far less dogmatic in his beliefs.

Thanks to Gereke’s strong relationship with the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>, a rural special-interest party, he has successfully negotiated a merger of the declining party into the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>, though only a few officials remain in the effectively dead party. His support for a public works program has stemmed criticism from the labor factions, and his ability to unite the key interest groups on which the Commonwealth Right depends on will help secure strong <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span> backing for the party.

Needless to say, this has not sat well with the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>’s Catholic wing, and has made cooperation within the party impossible for the foreseeable future.

@treviranus
title: Gottfried Trevannon, formerly of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span>, is elected as their new leader.
subtitle: The leader of the <span style="color: #0087DC;">Volkskonservativ</span> movement, and an advocate for democratic principles. - <span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservatives</span> and <span style="color: #000099;">Catholic Right</span> Wing
unavailable-subtitle: Trevannon has earned himself enemies to the right, and the Catholic portion of the party is reluctant to back him. - <span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservatives</span> and <span style="color: #000099;">Catholic Right</span> Wing
choose-if: treviranus_unlock
on-arrival: unionist_relation = 0 if unionist_relation < 0; concord_left += 3 if concord_ideology == "Right"; concord_right += 3 if concord_ideology == "Left"; nationalism += 3; pro_republic += 5; burgher_unionist += 6; guild_unionist += 4; landed_unionist -= 4; landed_dnf += 4; burgher_gold -= 4; burgher_lvp -= 4; burgher_ddp -= 2; guild_gold -= 4; guild_lvp -= 4; guild_ddp -= 2; burgher_dnf += 2; guild_dnf += 4; faithful_unionist += 2; concord_leader = "Trevannon"; concord_ideology = "Moderate"; guild_unionist = 25 if guild_unionist < 25; landed_unionist = 25 if landed_unionist < 25
face-image: img/portraits/Trevannon.jpg

Gottfried Trevannon[? if traditionalist_leader == "Trevannon":, the most recent leader of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?], leader of the thriving <span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservative</span> movement, is seen as the ideal candidate for the first chairman of the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>. His <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span> <span class="tooltip-text" title="that's me! the modman!">origin</span>, strong ties to key figures like Westmore on the right, and his careful cultivation of relations with the <span style="color: #000000;">Catholics</span> have earned him broad support for his leadership.

With his control of the colossally sized <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>, Trevannon has finally been able to mold it into the <span style="color: #0087DC;">Tory Democratic</span> party he has long envisioned. His extensive connections with Staal, Commonwealth industry[? if president == "DuFour":, President DuFour?], and the bourgeois elite are expected to greatly aid his leadership ambitions.

Despite his democratic leanings, the <span style="color: #000000;">[+ unionist_party_name +]</span> remains firmly opposed to <span style="color: #9B0000;">Marxism</span>, effectively ruling out any prospects of coalition with us.

@compromise
title: The vote has been deadlocked!
subtitle: No candidate is able to gather a sufficient amount of votes.
view-if: concord_deadlock
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.democratic_points > Q.presidential_points) {
    Q.democratic_points_lead = 1;
    if (Q.tory_democratic_points >= Q.unionist_points) {
        Q.tory_democratic_points_lead = 1;
        Q.catholic_center_points_lead = 0;
    } else if (Q.unionist_points > Q.tory_democratic_points) {
        Q.tory_democratic_points_lead = 0;
        Q.catholic_center_points_lead = 1;
    }
} else {
    Q.democratic_points_lead = 0;
}

if (Q.presidential_points > Q.democratic_points) {
    Q.presidential_points_lead = 1;
    if (!Q.labor_right_points_lead) {
        if (Q.conservative_right_points >= Q.labor_right_points && Q.conservative_right_points >= Q.agrarian_right_points) {
            Q.conservative_right_points_lead = 1;
            Q.agrarian_right_points_lead = 0;
            Q.labor_right_points_lead = 0;
        } else if (Q.labor_right_points >= Q.conservative_right_points && Q.labor_right_points >= Q.agrarian_right_points) {
            Q.conservative_right_points_lead = 0;
            Q.labor_right_points_lead = 1;
            Q.agrarian_right_points_lead = 0;
        } else if (Q.agrarian_right_points >= Q.conservative_right_points && Q.agrarian_right_points >= Q.labor_right_points) {
            Q.conservative_right_points_lead = 0;
            Q.labor_right_points_lead = 0;
            Q.agrarian_right_points_lead = 1;
        }
    }
} else {
    Q.presidential_points_lead = 0;
}

if (Q.democratic_points_lead && Q.tory_democratic_points_lead) {
    Q.goerdeler_unlock = 1;
} else if (Q.democratic_points_lead && Q.catholic_center_points_lead) {
    Q.bolz_unlock = 1;
} else if (Q.presidential_points_lead && Q.conservative_right_points_lead) {
    Q.westarp_unlock = 1;
} else if (Q.presidential_points_lead && !Q.conservative_right_points_lead) {
    Q.lejeune_jung_unlock = 1;
}

if (!Q.goerdeler_unlock && !Q.bolz_unlock && !Q.westarp_unlock && !Q.lejeune_jung_unlock || Q.unionist_votes - Q.bvp_votes < 20 || ((Q.year == 1931 && Q.month >= 11) && (Q.year == 1932 && Q.month == 1))) {
    if (!Q.goerdeler_unlock && !Q.bolz_unlock && !Q.westarp_unlock && !Q.lejeune_jung_unlock) {
        Q.vorbeck_deadlock = 1;
    } else if (Q.unionist_votes - Q.bvp_votes < 20) {
        Q.vorbeck_decline = 1;
    } else {
        Q.vorbeck_presidential = 1;
    }
    Q.vorbeck_unlock = 1;
    Q.westarp_unlock = 0;
    Q.lejeune_jung_unlock = 0;
    Q.bolz_unlock = 0;
    Q.goerdeler_unlock = 0;
}

!}

In the first few rounds of balloting, no candidate is able to rally a majority of the party behind themselves. With an impasse having settled, new compromise candidates have been proposed.

<span style="color: #003755;">Far-Right Protestants</span> (<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>) - ??? - [? if (concord_ideology != "Right" or royalist_votes < 35): Fringe ?][? if (concord_ideology == "Right" and royalist_votes >= 30): Marginal ?]

<span style="color: #3E3B2D;">Far-Right Catholics</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>) - ??? - [? if (concord_ideology != "Right" or royalist_votes < 30): Fringe ?][? if (concord_ideology == "Right" and royalist_votes >= 25): Marginal ?]

<span style="color: #3E88B3;">National Conservatives</span> (<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>) - Westmore / Lejeune-Jung / Goodlake - [? if concord_ideology == "Left": Marginal?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and not presidential_points_lead: Limited?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and presidential_points_lead: Influential?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and conservative_right_points_lead: Powerful?]

<span style="color: #385A38;">Agrarians</span> (<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>) - Westmore - [? if concord_ideology == "Left": Marginal?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and not presidential_points_lead: Limited?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and presidential_points_lead: Relevant?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and agrarian_right_points_lead: Influential?]
<hr id="read-marker">
<span style="color: #6D5298;">Christian Socials</span> (<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>) - Lethmoor - [? if concord_ideology == "Left" and not labor_points_lead: Marginal?][? if ((concord_ideology != "Left" and not presidential_points_lead) or (concord_ideology == "Left" and labor_points_lead)): Limited?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and presidential_points_lead and not labor_points_lead: Relevant?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and labor_points_lead: Influential?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and labor_right_points_lead: Powerful?]

<span style="color: #330000;">Catholic Labor</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>) - Bolz - [? if concord_ideology == "Left" and labor_left_points_lead: Powerful?][? if (concord_ideology == "Left" and not labor_left_points_lead) or labor_points_lead: Influential?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and democratic_points_lead and not labor_points_lead: Relevant?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and not democratic_points_lead and not labor_points_lead: Limited?]
<hr id="read-marker">
<span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservatives</span> (<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>) - Goodlake / Lethmoor - [? if concord_ideology == "Left" and democratic_points_lead: Dominant?][? if ((concord_ideology == "Left" and not democratic_points_lead) or (democratic_points_lead and concord_ideology != "Left")): Influential?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and not democratic_points_lead: Relevant?]

<span style="color: #000099;">Catholic Right</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>) - Lejeune-Jung / Bolz - [? if concord_ideology == "Left" and democratic_points_lead: Influential?][? if ((concord_ideology == "Left" and not democratic_points_lead) or (democratic_points_lead and concord_ideology != "Left")): Relevant?][? if concord_ideology == "Right" and not democratic_points_lead: Limited?]
<hr id="read-marker">
<span style="color: #000000;">the Unionists</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>) - Bolz / Lejeune-Jung - [? if concord_ideology == "Left" and democratic_points_lead: Powerful?][? if ((concord_ideology == "Left" and not democratic_points_lead) or (democratic_points_lead and concord_ideology != "Left")): Influential?][? if concord_ideology != "Left" and not democratic_points_lead: Relevant?]

<span style="color: #FF7F00;">Christian Left</span> (<span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>) - Bolz - [? if concord_ideology == "Left" and labor_left_points_lead: Relevant?][? if concord_ideology == "Left" and not labor_left_points_lead: Limited?][? if concord_ideology != "Left": Marginal?]
<hr id="read-marker">
All the compromise candidates that have emerged are broadly acceptable to the majority of the party, but a final decision on which to elect has yet to be made. Retired war hero and Assembly member Lethmoor has been suggested as a unity candidate, but persuading the reluctant Lethmoor to lead a political party would require far more than just factional support.

