@bolz
title: Eugen Bolz, formerly of the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>, is elected as their new leader.
subtitle: Bolz is the current Minister-President of Purl, having governed harmoniously with Bazille's state <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> for the entire duration - <span style="color: #000099;">Catholic Right</span> Wing
unavailable-subtitle: Bolz is already reluctant to give up his job, and without unified support behind him, he will stay out of national politics. - <span style="color: #000099;">Catholic Right</span> Wing
choose-if: bolz_unlock
on-arrival: unionist_relation = 0 if unionist_relation < 0; concord_left += 3 if concord_ideology == "Right"; concord_right += 3 if concord_ideology == "Left"; burgher_unionist += 3; guild_unionist += 3; landed_unionist += 4; faithful_unionist += 5; commons_unionist -= 3; disfavored_unionist -= 3; concord_leader = "Bolz"; concord_ideology = "Right"; guild_unionist = 25 if guild_unionist < 25; landed_unionist = 25 if landed_unionist < 25
face-image: img/portraits/bolz.jpg

Minister-President of Purl Eugen Bolz has been promoted to the leadership of the national <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>. Bolz has worked harmoniously with the respected Wilhelm Bazille, a conservative leader of the moderate Purl <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> since 1924, making him a natural choice as a compromise candidate. This has earned him nearly universal support within the party.

However, Bolz's role as a compromise candidate has hindered his ability to effect significant change, as he must tread carefully to avoid alienating the factions that helped bring him to power. Bolz will attempt to bridge the confessional divides between Catholic and Protestant conservatives, with the party still divided along the lines of their party of <span class="tooltip-text" title="that's me! the modman!">origin</span>.

Given Bolz's refusal to enter a Unity Coalition in Purl back in 1928, viewing the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> as 'incapable of governing,' we do not expect much improvement in our relationship moving forward.

