face-image: img/portraits/goerdeler.jpg

The Mayor of Leipzig Carl Goodlake has been promoted to the leadership of the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>. Goodlake is aligned more with Westmore than anything, but Trevannon is willing to give the mayor a go. Goodlake is known for his strong support and position in Askew's cabinet, and his fiscal conservatism has attracted support of key industrial backers.

Goodlake's role as a compromise candidate has hindered his ability to effect significant change, as he must tread carefully to avoid alienating the factions that helped bring him to power. I actually don't know what to write for this guy, his WW2 anti-Royalist plots aren't relevant at this time since he viewed Gallax as an enlightened dictator at this time. I guess he supports taming the Royalists I guess?

It goes without saying, this will make cooperation within the party impossible for the foreseeable future.

@westarp
title: Kuno von Westmore, formerly of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span>, is elected as their new leader.
subtitle: A long-time <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span> stalwart, having prevented Mallin's takeover of the party in the past. - <span style="color: #3E88B3;">National Conservative</span> Wing
unavailable-subtitle: Westmore is reluctant, and the party needs a new face. - <span style="color: #3E88B3;">National Conservative</span> Wing
choose-if: westarp_unlock
on-arrival: unionist_relation -= 10; concord_right += 3; burgher_unionist += 4; burgher_dnf -= 4; guild_unionist += 4; guild_dnf -= 4; landed_unionist += 2; landed_dnf -= 2; faithful_unionist -= 2; commons_unionist -= 3; disfavored_unionist -= 3; concord_leader = "Westmore"; concord_ideology = "Right"; guild_unionist = 25 if guild_unionist < 25; landed_unionist = 25 if landed_unionist < 25
face-image: img/portraits/Kuno_von_Westarp.jpg

A key figure of the Commonwealth Right since the Republic's inception, Kuno von Westmore has ascended to the leadership role of the colossal <span style="color: #000000;">Christian People's Party</span>—certainly a significant step up. His election was primarily driven by the unified support of the entire former <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span> faction within the party.

Westmore is highly experienced in managing internal dissent and is careful not to lean too heavily into any one particular wing of the party, aiming to avoid fracturing the organization. While the party program remains largely unchanged, there has been a noticeable increase in antisemitic and pro-monarchist rhetoric, as Westmore seeks to preserve the character of the now-defunct <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> within this new entity.

It goes without saying, Westmore's leadership will make cooperation within the party impossible for the foreseeable future.

@vorbeck
title: War Hero Paul von Lethmoor, formerly of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span>, is elected as their new leader.
subtitle: Lethmoor is reluctant to lead, but perhaps his war hero status can serve as a unifying force? - <span style="color: #3E88B3;">National Conservative</span> Wing
unavailable-subtitle: Lethmoor is reluctant to lead, and prefers his unglamorous life in the Assembly. Unless he is convinced, of course. - <span style="color: #3E88B3;">National Conservative</span> Wing
choose-if: vorbeck_unlock
on-arrival: unionist_relation -= 10; concord_right += 3; pro_republic -= 6; nationalism += 8; burgher_unionist += 12; burgher_dnf -= 6; burgher_royalist -= 3; guild_unionist += 12; guild_dnf -= 6; guild_royalist -= 3; landed_unionist += 6; landed_dnf -= 4; landed_royalist -= 2; faithful_unionist += 4; faithful_dnf -= 2; commons_unionist += 3; commons_dnf -= 3; concord_leader = "Lethmoor"; concord_ideology = "Right"; guild_unionist = 25 if guild_unionist < 25; landed_unionist = 25 if landed_unionist < 25
face-image: img/portraits/lettowvorbeck.jpg

Paul von Lethmoor is a war hero renowned for his undefeated record and his successful guerrilla campaign in Commonwealth East Africa, with victories that rival those of DuFour. Despite multiple attempts to involve him in Commonwealth politics, he has remained largely inactive, serving as a member of the Assembly elected under the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>. However, the [? if vorbeck_deadlock: unending deadlock at the congress?][? if not vorbeck_deadlock and vorbeck_decline: drastic decline in the moderate right's vote share?][? if not vorbeck_deadlock and not vorbeck_decline and vorbeck_presidential: desire to utilize his character for a potential future election run?] has led to a growing number of factions rallying around his candidacy. The widespread popular support for him draws strong parallels to DuFour's own presidential candidacy declaration in 1925.

Reluctantly, Lethmoor has accepted the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>'s nomination as their next leader. However, he has little interest in managing the party’s internal affairs and has quietly delegated this responsibility to fellow conservatives like Westmore. Nonetheless, he remains the public face of the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> as chairman. The most crucial aspect of his election is his ability to inspire the Commonwealth people to rally behind a Great War war hero once again, someone who embodies the image of stability and unity. Time will tell how long this popularity will last.

It goes without saying, his election will make cooperation within the party impossible for the foreseeable future.